From: Kenichi Ishibashi <bashi@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 22:44:51 -0700
Subject: [M152] Abort navigation on overlapping redirect or response

Original change's description:
> Abort navigation on overlapping redirect or response
>
> In NavigationURLLoaderImpl, receiving an OnReceiveRedirect or
> OnReceiveResponse IPC while another exclusive task is in flight (such as
> asynchronous header parsing for an earlier redirect) violates the
> URLLoaderClient protocol.
>
> Previously, these entry points guarded against this using only
> DUMP_WILL_BE_CHECK(!loader_holder_.HasExclusiveTask()). In builds where
> DUMP_WILL_BE_CHECK is non-fatal, an untrusted or compromised Network
> Service could send overlapping OnReceiveRedirect calls. This overwrote
> redirect_info_ with the new redirect target while NavigationRequest was
> still asynchronously vetting the earlier redirect. When NavigationRequest
> subsequently called FollowRedirect(), NavigationURLLoaderImpl followed
> the unvetted target.
>
> This CL fixes the issue by:
> 1. Immediately terminating the navigation with net::ERR_UNEXPECTED if
>    loader_holder_.HasExclusiveTask() is true in OnReceiveRedirect().
> 2. Adding an identical guard to OnReceiveResponse() to prevent desync
>    if a response arrives while an exclusive task is in progress.
> 3. In OnReceiveRedirect's error path, allowing LoaderHolder::State::kNone
>    alongside kLoadingViaReceiver when url_loader() is null.
> 4. Adding unit tests in NavigationURLLoaderImplTest covering overlapping
>    redirects during header parsing, overlapping redirects while throttle
>    checks are pending, and responses arriving during redirect header parsing.
>
